\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
A graph $H$ is forcing if its expected homomorphism density together with edge density forces quasirandomness of a graph sequence. Are the forcing graphs exactly the bipartite graphs containing a cycle?
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2011/01}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
A graph $H$ is forcing if its expected homomorphism density together with edge density forces quasirandomness of a graph sequence. Are the forcing graphs exactly the bipartite graphs containing a cycle?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems, record 30001661 (OWR-4791-019). Catalogue attribution under CC BY 4.0.
